            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is delicious dip. It is so much better than recipes with the Knorr Vegetable Soup Mix because the ingredients are all fresh. This is a great way to eat spinach and so healthy!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "addles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used fresh cooked/chopped spinach not frozen (had 5 lbs to use up and made 3 dif recipes with spinach), had to use garlic powder instead of fresh, (1/8 tsp per clove though I used half a tsp), used red onions, and subbed in some tiny red and green pickled peppers (all I had pepper wise here). Let it sit overnight then tried it tonight and oh my gosh. First time making spinach dip and this is simply amazing. Trust me and let it marinate longer than it says. You will be rewarded.",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-22T00:41:30.970Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachel Lee Naasz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe, though I make a lot of changes. I sautée the onion and bell peppers, otherwise their flavors drown out the flavor of the spinach. I also use less mayonnaise and sour cream to make it healthier; I use about 1/4 -1/3 cups each. I double the amount of cumin and will sometimes add a 1/2 cup of any shredded or grated white cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-30T13:18:13.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mike Ralls"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Cut out the fresh onion and used 1/2 pack Lipton Onion Soup mix. Added 2oz can water chestnuts coarse chop. Added two med carrots shredded fine. Added tsp lime juice, added 1/2 tsp ground red pepper.",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-19T21:31:44.510Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vanessa Hess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this dip. It's a nice departure from the artichoke and cheese spinach dips. I use green onions with this as I find the mild flavor is delicious with the spinach. I also like to drain and touch chop a can of sliced water chestnuts to add for some crunch. Celery would also work but may alter the flavor profile some. I took this for a work potluck and the bowl was scraped clean!! I have also successfully made this using vegan sour cream and mayo for family that had dietary restrictions and they asked for the recipe. I have also added sun dried tomatoes to it for a fun twist and it was delicious. Thank you for this delicious recipe! It a fav for me!!",
            "datePublished": "2016-10-28T01:41:53.770Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ndwife"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this! Used 1/4 onion, whole orange pepper, 2 tsp. granulated garlic, and fresh spinach.",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-18T19:38:40.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cecilia8240"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a nice dip, but I'd suggest adding a little lemon or lime juice as this really brightens the dish. Also, I'd make it a day in advance: I found that the cumin flavor really comes through after the dip sat in the fridge overnight. Thanks for the recipe, jen.",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-03T20:42:40.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Liz McLaughlin Deal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use grated carrot instead of red bell pepper and also add chopped water chestnuts for crunch. Everyone who has tasted this LOVES it! Garlic is strong so be prepared or tweak for your own taste.\n\nYummy with Fritos scoops.",
            "datePublished": "2015-10-17T10:34:28.293Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "skweeky"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made several changes, based I what I had on hand. I use greek yogurt instead of sour cream, no bell pepper, one clove of garlic, less onion and I added dill and Montreal steak seasoning.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-10T08:46:27.147Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bowline"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Everyone loved it, I will make it again. I did use 3/4 yogurt and a 1/4 mayonnaise; When I make it again I will use all yogurt instead for a healthier dip.",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-22T10:36:04.930Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "smhayley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The onion is super strong, so I would suggest half an onion, cooking the onion, or using green onion instead. The flavor is best if sitting in the fridge for a few hours, but still good for the time in the directions. It's my go-to quick spinach dip. If you want a little more flavor, add some cheese to the hot spinach before adding the rest of the ingredients.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-10T13:43:58.217Z"
          },
          {
